what's going on everybody welcome back  to the cosmic wonder I'm your host  Warren Thompson and black panther  wakanda forever is officially out in  theaters today we're going to be going  over a little bit of the ending but  breaking down that post-credit scene so  if you have not seen the movie and you  are trying to avoid spoilers this is  your official spoiler alert now most  likely if you are still here you have  seen the movie or you simply don't care  about spoilers but if you have seen the  movie let us know in the comments down  below what you thought about it you can  rank it between 1 to 10 or a to F or  simply just give us your thoughts about  it now black panther wakanda forever was  obviously a really really big movie for  a lot of reasons the biggest of course  being the fact that we lost Chadwick  Boseman who played Black Panther slash  t'challa it's incredibly sad and of  course he will be missed by everybody  his death came as a huge shock to pretty  much everybody except his immediate  family surrounding him he didn't even  tell the people over at Marvel Studios  that he had cancer so when he passed  away it was a big shock not only to the  world but to Marvel Studios as well even  the director of the first black panther  and black panther wakanda forever didn't  know he shared recently that he finally  finished the Black Panther 2 script  which of course had Chadwick in it at  the time he asked Chadwick Boseman if he  wanted to look at it before he sent it  to the studio in which Chadwick said no  but Ryan coogler has stated in an  interview he thought that Chadwick felt  too tired to read it Ryan coogler went  on to say Chadwick Boseman would die  about two weeks later now shortly after  the passing of Chadwick Boseman Marvel  Studios came out and we listened to  president Kevin feige tell us that they  decided to not recast t'challa slash the  Black Panther in the MCU now whether or  not people agreed with this decision or  not I think most people understood why  Marvel Studios decided to do this  however there was still a big movement  out there calling for the recasting of  t'challa because how much the character  means to a lot of people plus not to  mention there are a ton of stories that  you can do in the MCU but in the comics  are heavily revolved around t'challa  well in this post those credit scene  they kind of found a way to still please  the fans a way to bring t'challa back  into the Marvel Cinematic Universe but  also a way that gives us time to mourn  the death of Chadwick in Black Panther  wakanda forever the movie starts off  with a scene of shuri actually trying to  recreate a synthetic heart-shaped herb  because her brother King t'challa is  dying however sadly Queen ramonda comes  in and tells shuri that her brother is  gone they say he died from an unknown  illness and we have a funeral for King  t'challa and this movie is very much  about not only the characters grieving  but also the actors as well in fact  there are sometimes in the movie where  you can't tell if they are acting or  simply grieving for a friend so in the  post-credits scene we see shuri burning  the Robes of t'challa something that she  was going to do with her mother earlier  on in the movie as a part of the  grieving process and as a way to move on  shuri becomes the New Black Panther in  this film so the mantle of the Black  Panther is still there however with King  t'challa gone the character t'challa was  gone as well until Marvel figured out a  great way to to still have a t'challa in  the Marvel Cinematic Universe in the  movie we find out that Nakia is living  in Haiti at one point in time Nakia  tells shuri she's always welcome at her  house and at the very end of the film we  see Sherry go to nakia's house which is  on the beach and shuri goes down to the  beach and performs the ritual we have a  really nice scene here paying tribute to  Chadwick Boseman and t'challa showing us  clips from Black Panther 1 and this  shows us shuri going through the  grieving process and essentially finally  deciding to move on the movie ends here  but the post-credit picks up right after  in the same exact scene we see Nakia  come out and greet shuri on the beach  but she has somebody with her a young  boy and she tells that young boy that  shuri is his aunt she says that his name  is tassant but then he tells shuri that  my mom says you can keep a secret and he  says that tosantis is Haitian name and  his real name is actually t'challa and  this is where it is revealed that Nakia  and t'challa had a son together and this  is their son he even says I am Prince  t'challa son of King t'challa this comes  as a pretty big shock to shuri but of  course it is an extremely happy moment  and not gonna lie it got me pretty good  in the theater but from here Nokia  explains that King t'challa said that he  didn't want to raise his son in the  Kingdom but he actually did prepare  Nakia and his son t'chella for his death  throughout the movie where Nokia comes  back she meets many different characters  along the way that she hasn't seen in a  very long time like koi Queen ramonda  and shuri they each expressed that they  missed her at the funeral however if you  notice shuri and akoyi were a little  hurt that they didn't see her at the  funeral however Queen raimonda simply  says that she missed her this is because  as we find out t'challa and Nakia told  the queen about their son and queen  raimonda actually met their son as well  Nakia reveals to Sherry that t'challa  told them not to visit the funeral  because if they visited the funeral  instead of focusing on grieving and  saying their goodbyes to King t'chella  they would be more surprised and taken  back by the fact that t'challa has a son  and that they kept him from him for all  these years but Queen raimonda knew this  so instead of being kind of hurt by the  fact that Nakia did not attend the  funeral she simply says that she missed  her so I think this is a pretty great  move by Marvel Studios because now we do  essentially have a recasting of t'challa  in the Marvel Cinematic Universe and  recently with black panther wakanda  forever coming out of course they've  been doing a ton of interviews leading  up to the movie and Kevin feige has  revealed that the reason that they did  not recast t'challa for black panther 2  was because they felt it was too soon so  this basically confirmed that they  didn't think that they weren't going to  ever recast t'challa simply they did not  recast him for the specific black  panther wakanda forever movie because  now in the post-credits scene it's very  clear that they in their own way have  recast t'challa this t'challa will  essentially go on to become the same  character which is really great because  we have everything that Chadwick Boseman  gave us as his t'challa but now with  this new one his son will get to see  many different storylines play out in  the MCU that have played out in the  comics that fans really really want to  see the X-Men are now making their way  to the MCU and a big storyline in the  comics is the marriage between the X-Men  Storm and King t'challa they also do go  on to have a son together in the comics  and now that we again have a t'challa in  the MCU all these storylines are  possible whereas they were not before  it's most likely that we're going to see  somewhat of a time Jump with t'challa  although hopefully not too big of a time  Jump because now it's possible for  t'challa to actually go on to become a  young Avenger Marvel has been setting up  the Young Avengers for quite some time  now in the MCU so this would be a really  really cool opportunity to have a young  t'challa be a part of the Young Avengers  team then eventually do a Time jump  again and have him grow up to become the  king of wakanda and take the  heart-shaped herb and become the Black  Panther I'm sure shuri will always kind  of keep the mantle of the Black Panther  this did happen in the comics and there  is totally room for two black panthers  in the Marvel Cinematic Universe right  now or it could be that when t'challa  finally becomes of age to be king of  wakanda shuri would step down from the  Black black panther mantle and let her  nephew have it there are also other  major stories involving Namor that we  could see in the MCU again as well like  The Avengers vs the X-Men which still  also ties into storm the Phoenix Force  possesses the Phoenix 5 and Namor ends  up flooding wakanda killing a lot of  people kind of what we saw in Black  Panther wakanda forever however t'challa  is on the side of the Avengers and his  wife storm is on the side of the X-Men  and after the flooding of wakanda black  panther tells his wife storm that he  wants a divorce but in the comics the  wedding between t'challa and storm is a  really big deal everybody comes to watch  it and even The Watcher himself shows up  to witness the ceremony so by Marvel  Studios deciding to essentially not  recast t'challa right away but now bring  in another t'challa this is their way of  recasting the character and now all of  these story options are available moving  forward in the MCU it's definitely a  really really happy ending for a really  sad situation Chadwick Boseman and  t'challa were definitely definitely  missed in this film their absence was  very felt but I think he would have felt  pretty great about how the movie came  out and how they're going forward with  t'challa in the MCU but hey let me know  your thoughts about this in the comments  down below what did you think about the  movie and what do you think about the  way they're going about recasting the  character t'challa let us know in the  comments and don't forget to like the  video and subscribe so you don't miss  out on any of the latest news for live  updates you can follow me on Instagram  and Twitter and as always thank you all  so much for watching woof woof
 

